    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1005">

                <pb facs="1163" n="1051" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1051"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.797/15: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-24T13:00:00-05:00">December 24, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>202. Your 247, December 19, 5 p.m.</p>
                <pb facs="1164" n="1052" xml:id="pg1052"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Department has no objection to exploratory conversations with Kurusu
                        in regard to details of the draft legislation.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>While leaving the matter to the Embassy’s judgment, the Department
                        inclines to the opinion that, if the proposed legislation conforms to the
                        Embassy’s 1440, August 22,<anchor n="21" xml:id="d1005-f1"/> an oral
                        statement as authorized in the final paragraph of the Department’s 882,
                        November 18, would be desirable.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
